# the sink out of a worker thread. `json.dumps` has `ensure_ascii=True`, so both planes must
# write `\uXXXX` -- and this is the scenario that proves the C++ escaper matches rather than
# only its unit check.
scenario vietnamese_camera
camera cầu-cảng-01
frame 3
source shard-2
size 640 480
# 12.5 is a real camera rate and the one place the two rounding rules differ: Python's
# `round` is half TO EVEN (12) while `llround` is half away from zero (13). The gate
# carries it so the boundary is compared and not merely unit-checked.
fps 12.5
reason complete

